From: Mason Morris <masonmorris8@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:44:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] Map HRTF directions onto the HRIR sphere's axes

The panner swapped y and z when it handed the source direction to the hrtf
crate, so elevation went to the sphere's front axis and front-back to its
up axis. Horizontal sources were looked up on the sphere's vertical circle,
and only sources straight to the left or right got the right response. The
IRCAM spheres have the front at -z, up at +y and the left at -x; map to
those.
---
 src/node/panner.rs | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/node/panner.rs b/src/node/panner.rs
index 2663579..8c5ee5b 100644
--- a/src/node/panner.rs
+++ b/src/node/panner.rs
@@ -240,10 +240,12 @@ impl HrtfState {
         // reset state of output buffer
         self.output_interleaved.fill((0., 0.));
 
+        // The HRIR spheres have the front at -z, up at +y and the left at -x, so a source in
+        // front lands at -z and an elevated one at +y.
         let new_sample_vector = Vec3 {
             x: projected_source[0],
-            z: projected_source[1],
-            y: projected_source[2],
+            y: projected_source[1],
+            z: -projected_source[2],
         };
 
         let context = HrtfContext {
